{{Quote|No more explosives. I didn't sign off on bombing Garsa's Sanctuary. I agreed to surgical strikes, not open warfare.|[[Mok Shaiz]], to the Pyke boss|<ref name="In the Name of Honor">{{BOBF|Chapter 7: In the Name of Honor}}</ref>}}
'''Garsa Fwip's Sanctuary''',<ref name="Insider 224">{{InsiderCite|224|Hit it, Max!}}</ref> also known simply as the '''Sanctuary''', was a [[cantina]],<ref name="Stranger in a Strange Land" /> upscale club, and [[casino]]<ref name="World Building">{{InsiderCite|227|World Building (Star Wars Insider 227)}}</ref> located in [[Mos Espa]], [[Tatooine]], during the [[New Republic Era]]. The [[Gender|female]] [[Twi'lek]] Madam [[Garsa Fwip]] owned the cantina.<ref name="Stranger in a Strange Land" /> The establishment was complete with a bar, gambling tables, and live music, and was even alive with helmet cleaning. At least two individuals were employed there, a [[Unidentified Twi'lek male server|male Twi'lek server]] and a [[Unidentified Twi'lek female server|female Twi'lek server]]. The cantina was [[Destruction of Garsa Fwip's Sanctuary|destroyed]] when two members of the [[Pyke Syndicate]] left a bomb, disguised as a [[camtono]].<ref name="Chapter 6">{{BOBF|Chapter 6: From the Desert Comes a Stranger}}</ref>

{{Struct-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
The Sanctuary first appeared in "[[Chapter 1: Stranger in a Strange Land]]," the first episode of the live-action television series ''[[Star Wars: The Book of Boba Fett]]''.<ref name="Stranger in a Strange Land" />

